This is sort of suspicious.

>Using fallback locale: UTF-8

@reporter also, it seems like you haven't enabled the `print_events` log?

@participant1 @participant2 

Here is a new log file with `print-events` set to `true`. Alacritty **not** started from terminal, after Alacritty started I type the letters `asdf` on german keyboard layout:

[Alacritty-99660.log](https://github.com/alacritty/alacritty/files/11077787/Alacritty-99660.log)

@participant11 
> Potentially related: `window.option_as_alt` seems to completely break input if I set it to something other than None and attempt to type something that requires pressing option to type. (e.g. @ on apple's nordic layout).

check https://github.com/alacritty/alacritty/issues/6720 and "macOS Alt/Option situation" entry in https://github.com/alacritty/alacritty/releases/tag/v0.12.0-rc1

@participant11 
I have a portuguese layout keyboard and in my alacrity.yml :

```
window:
  option_as_alt: Both

key_bindings:
  - { key: LBracket,      mods: Alt,            chars: "\x5B"                }
  - { key: RBracket,      mods: Alt,            chars: "\x5D"               }
  - { key: Key2,             mods: Alt,            chars: "\x40"               }
  - { key: Key3,             mods: Alt,            chars: "€"                    }
  - { key: LBracket,      mods: Alt|Shift,      chars: "\x7B"             }
  - { key: RBracket,      mods: Alt|Shift,      chars: "\x7D"            }
```

and everything works perfectly (for me since RC2)! I use alacritty alone, with tmux and several editors (Emacs, Helix) locally and via ssh and 0.12 is the best release until now! No eated keys nor nothing similar to the mains issue described.

Hello guys,

I have found to have the same issue here, but not all the time, only when changing from romaji and japanese（For those don't know there's a special key for that) some times. And my settings are following the guide on the changelog. Found though that ~changing the keyboard layout to let's say "us layout" and put back restores the input~.

~Can some one guide me how to find the alacritty log file? So I put in here too.~
Was wrote [up in the thread](https://github.com/alacritty/alacritty/issues/6817#issuecomment-1483920054), sorry.

macOS: Monterey 12.6.4

